<!--
  Tells search engines which pages exist and matter.

  The homepage, and the three sample documents linked from it. app.html is
  the Workspace: it needs an account, so there is nothing there for a
  search result to show, and a thin login page competing with the homepage
  helps nobody.

  The PDFs are listed because they answer a question people actually
  search — what a script breakdown, a shooting schedule or a call sheet
  looks like — and they are the only Slate output readable without an
  account. A crawler would find them by following the links anyway;
  listing them gets them fetched sooner.

  lastmod is the date the page last changed in a way worth re-reading.
  Update it when the homepage changes substantially; it does not need
  touching for a typo. The PDFs' lastmod is the date of the run that
  produced them — change it only if the samples are regenerated.
-->
